Option: redirects-B
Name: Old farm addresses: 13 small "this page has moved" pages, in the visitor's language
Does: Adds 13 folders (about/, contact/, faq/, food/ ...), each with an index.html that jumps to the matching page or section, lets tools/make_deploy_folder.py upload them, and lets tools/launch_check.py see that such a page forwards (it counts only real redirects otherwise). For hosts that ignore _redirects. Not a true 301: Google may take longer to move over. The two lines on each page are translated like any page text: data-t ids, the translations in lang/src, and tools/i18n.py reads these folders. js/moved.js shows them in the visitor's language before the first line is drawn (?lang=, else the language saved with the language button, else the browser's list; English stays if the words do not arrive, and without JavaScript). The jump itself is unchanged.
Answers: d30 A (old addresses), d05 (any host; the only choice on GitHub Pages)
Group: redirects
Conflicts: redirects-A
Requires: tools/launch_check.py, tools/make_deploy_folder.py and tools/i18n.py in the site (it edits all three)
Host: any
Order: 30
After: python3 tools/pages.py, then python3 tools/i18n.py extract, then python3 tools/i18n.py jsstrings, then python3 tools/i18n.py build, then python3 tools/i18n.py missing es hi zh vi (0 missing each); upload again (python3 tools/make_deploy_folder.py includes the folders)
Strings: 10 new texts (ids t1cfe894a ("This page has moved."), td571e817, t40ab10f5, tcf68a859, t931b0dae, tebcb6448, t3bf45e4b, t47f021a8, t5289f86c, t210e3b10), already translated into es, hi, zh, vi inside this patch (needs a native reader): the line "This page has moved." and 9 "Go to ..." link lines

